# traffic_light.logi: the smallest idea. One crossing, one light; the agent turns it red when asked.
# Try it:  logi try traffic_light.logi
name: traffic-light
about: a pedestrian crossing

== 1. conversation
client: c1 is a crossing
agent:  What colour is the light at c1?
client: the light at c1 is green
client: yes
agent:  Now: nothing is safe to cross.
client: make c1 safe to cross
agent:  Done: the light at c1 is red (command: lights c1 red).

== 2. facts
crossing(C) = {C} is a crossing
light(C, V) = the light at {C} is {V} | the light at {C} turns {V}   [changes; V: green amber red]

== 3. rules
safe(C)     = {C} is safe to cross
safe(C) :- crossing(C), light(C, red).

== 4. meta-interpreters
-- execute
act(light(C, V), [lights, C, V]).
# no can_change/1: by default the agent may change any fact that changes (here, the light)
-- complete
missing(light(C, _)) :- crossing(C), \+ light(C, _).
ask(light(C, _), ['What colour is the light at', C, '?']).
